## CRITICAL API Reference — Sparkline Creation (use these EXACT APIs)

The Sparkline types are in the `Aspose.Cells.Charts` namespace. You MUST add `using Aspose.Cells.Charts;` at the top of every code block.

### Correct sparkline creation pattern:

```csharp
using System;
using Aspose.Cells;
using Aspose.Cells.Charts;

Workbook workbook = new Workbook();
Worksheet worksheet = workbook.Worksheets[0];

// Populate sample data
worksheet.Cells["A1"].PutValue(5);
worksheet.Cells["B1"].PutValue(-3);
worksheet.Cells["C1"].PutValue(8);
worksheet.Cells["D1"].PutValue(-2);
worksheet.Cells["E1"].PutValue(6);

// Add a Line sparkline at F1
CellArea lineArea = new CellArea();
lineArea.StartColumn = 5;  // Column F (0-indexed)
lineArea.EndColumn = 5;
lineArea.StartRow = 0;     // Row 1 (0-indexed)
lineArea.EndRow = 0;
int lineIdx = worksheet.SparklineGroups.Add(SparklineType.Line, "A1:E1", false, lineArea);

// Add a Column sparkline at G1
CellArea columnArea = new CellArea();
columnArea.StartColumn = 6;  // Column G
columnArea.EndColumn = 6;
columnArea.StartRow = 0;
columnArea.EndRow = 0;
int columnIdx = worksheet.SparklineGroups.Add(SparklineType.Column, "A1:E1", false, columnArea);

// Add a Win/Loss sparkline at H1
// NOTE: SparklineType.Stacked is the correct enum for win/loss (NOT "WinLoss")
CellArea stackedArea = new CellArea();
stackedArea.StartColumn = 7;  // Column H
stackedArea.EndColumn = 7;
stackedArea.StartRow = 0;
stackedArea.EndRow = 0;
int stackedIdx = worksheet.SparklineGroups.Add(SparklineType.Stacked, "A1:E1", false, stackedArea);
```

### Converting each Sparkline to image and embedding (use Sparklines[0], NOT foreach):

Since each group is anchored at a single cell, each group has exactly one sparkline. Access it directly via `Sparklines[0]` — do NOT use a `foreach` loop.

`Sparkline.ToImage()` takes TWO parameters and returns `void` (it writes to a stream/file):
- `void Sparkline.ToImage(Stream stream, ImageOrPrintOptions options)` — writes image to stream
- `void Sparkline.ToImage(string fileName, ImageOrPrintOptions options)` — writes to file

```csharp
using System.IO;
using Aspose.Cells.Rendering;
using Aspose.Cells.Drawing;  // Required for ImageType enum

ImageOrPrintOptions imageOptions = new ImageOrPrintOptions();
imageOptions.ImageType = ImageType.Png;  // ImageType is in Aspose.Cells.Drawing namespace

// Convert the Line sparkline (group has exactly one sparkline) and embed in F2
Sparkline lineSp = worksheet.SparklineGroups[lineIdx].Sparklines[0];
using (MemoryStream ms = new MemoryStream())
{
    lineSp.ToImage(ms, imageOptions);
    worksheet.Cells["F2"].EmbeddedImage = ms.ToArray();
}

// Convert the Column sparkline and embed in G2
Sparkline columnSp = worksheet.SparklineGroups[columnIdx].Sparklines[0];
using (MemoryStream ms = new MemoryStream())
{
    columnSp.ToImage(ms, imageOptions);
    worksheet.Cells["G2"].EmbeddedImage = ms.ToArray();
}

// Convert the Win/Loss sparkline and embed in H2
Sparkline stackedSp = worksheet.SparklineGroups[stackedIdx].Sparklines[0];
using (MemoryStream ms = new MemoryStream())
{
    stackedSp.ToImage(ms, imageOptions);
    worksheet.Cells["H2"].EmbeddedImage = ms.ToArray();
}
```

### Key API notes:
- Access sparklines via `worksheet.SparklineGroups` (NOT `SparklineGroupCollection` or `SparklineGroupList`)
- `SparklineGroups.Add(SparklineType, string dataRange, bool isVertical, CellArea destArea)` returns an int index
- The third parameter `isVertical`: `false` = horizontal data range (row), `true` = vertical data range (column)
- `SparklineType.Line` for line sparklines
- `SparklineType.Column` for column sparklines
- **`SparklineType.Stacked` for win/loss sparklines** (the enum name is "Stacked" but it renders as win/loss — there is NO `SparklineType.WinLoss`)
- `CellArea` is a struct with `StartRow`, `EndRow`, `StartColumn`, `EndColumn` fields (all 0-indexed)
- Each `SparklineGroup` has a `.Sparklines` collection; since each group here is anchored at one cell, use `group.Sparklines[0]` to get the single sparkline
- `Sparkline.ToImage(Stream stream, ImageOrPrintOptions options)` returns `void` — it writes the image to the stream. Use `MemoryStream.ToArray()` to get bytes.
- `Cell.EmbeddedImage` is a `byte[]` property — assign the image bytes directly

